          "id": "0c992055d44e6d2537629802cfb20114439c6e32",
          "message": "CBMC: Call mld_randombytes by contract in crypto_sign_keypair\n\nFor the crypto_sign_keypair, the wrong function name was used in the\nUSE_FUNCTION_CONTRACTS. mld_randombytes() is the function that comes with a\ncontract which internally calls randombytes() which does not have a contract.\nIn consequence, CBMC would inline mlk_randombytes, which forwards to\nrandombytes which has no contract attached to it. Being asked to call\nrandombytes by contract, CBMC would create an empty contract rather than\nfailing.\n\nIn consequence, the CBMC proofs previously did not check the validity of the\noutput buffer passed to mlk_randombytes.\n\nThis commit fixes the issue by changing randombytes to mlk_randombytes in the\nCBMC Makefile.\n\nSigned-off-by: Matthias J. Kannwischer <matthias@kannwischer.eu>",
          "timestamp": "2025-11-07T22:23:14+08:00",
          "tree_id": "82d86ea8014a1bc01a24cdb01c8c52c4932be85a",
