          "id": "81c7c9a929dab92120eb17e9a9caf8db3b2929a0",
          "message": "Align mld_ct_memcmp with mlkem-native\n\nThe previous version of mld_ct_memp had a misplaced value\nbarrier allowing the compiler to elide part of the loop\ndesigned to prevent an early abort. We have not seen a\ncompiler placing an early abort without this prevention,\nbut as-is the code makes no sense.\n\nThis commit aligns mld_ct_memcmp with mlk_ct_memcmp from\nmlkem-native and adds the necessary cmask helpers and their\nCBMC proofs. We also slightly strengthen the spec to include\nthat the return value is either 0x00 or 0xFF. Previously,\nwe had only documented that it's 0 for equal data, and _some_\nnon-zero value otherwise. This needs to be backported\nto mlkem-native.\n\nNote the minor difference with mlkem-native that ct_cmask_nonzero_u8\nis built atop ct_cmask_nonzero_u32, rather than ct_cmask_nonzero_u16\nas in mlkem-native. This is more natural in the context of mldsa-native\nwhere most arithmetic is 32-bit.\n\nSigned-off-by: Hanno Becker <beckphan@amazon.co.uk>",
          "timestamp": "2026-01-03T22:07:34+08:00",
          "tree_id": "91eb4f1de66528f3a017481bfd88034e08263fb1",
