          "id": "4792f0ff3d5bb02340a5ccc723f1fc4bd647b701",
          "message": "sign.c: zeroize buffers in all code paths\n\nIn various functions in sign.c, the zeroization would only happen in case the\nfunction returned correctly. In the case of failure, there would be a shortcut\nthat returns without zeroization.\nThis commit fixes that ensuring zeroization for all code paths.\n\nSigned-off-by: Matthias J. Kannwischer <matthias@kannwischer.eu>\nSigned-off-by: Hanno Becker <beckphan@amazon.co.uk>",
