          "id": "9708948bb4f7a45ed3e9651323d124cbff3ecf8b",
          "message": "Examples: multilevel build\n\n- This commit add a multilevel build example demonstrating how to build\n  mldsa-native with support for all three security levels while sharing\n  level-independent code.\n\n- The example builds the library three times in separate build\n  directories(build/mldsa{44,65,87}).\n  ML-DSA-44 is built with MLD_CONFIG_MULTILEVEL_WITH_SHARED to include\n  all level-independent code, while ML-DSA-65 and ML-DSA-87 are built\n  with MLD_CONFIG_MULTILEVEL_NO_SHARED to exclude shared code.\n  All builds use the common namespace prefix 'mldsa' with automatic\n  suffixes (44/65/87) for level-dependent functions.\n\n- This commit made following changes:\n- Add examples/multilevel_build/ with:\n  - Makefile: Build system for all three security levels\n  - main.c: Test program exercising all three ML-DSA variants\n  - mldsa_native_all.h: Unified header exposing all three APIs\n  - expected_signatures.h: For validation\n  - README.md: Documentation\n  - Symlinks to mldsa source and test RNG\n- Add MULTILEVEL_BUILD test type in scripts/tests\n- Add multilevel_build to tests script\n- Add clean target for multilevel_build in root Makefile\n\n- reference from mlkem-native's multilevel_build example.\n\nSigned-off-by: willieyz <willie.zhao@chelpis.com>",
          "timestamp": "2025-12-02T11:30:28+08:00",
