          "distinct": true,
          "id": "40a44585c2d0f0672aec0eb1641e4f864c49c957",
          "message": "Make value barrier volatile\n\nThis commit modifies the definition of the standard value barrier\nby adding a `volatile` qualifier. Otherwise, there is risk the\ncompiler could correlate input and output merely from the fact that\nthe value barrier is deterministic. We have not seen this happening,\nbut it appears safer nontheless to add a volatile qualifier.\n\nSigned-off-by: Hanno Becker <beckphan@amazon.co.uk>",
          "timestamp": "2026-01-01T15:20:35+08:00",
